# MAGIC <div class="hero"><div class="blob b1"></div><div class="blob b2"></div><div class="blob b3"></div><div class="hero-in"><div class="kicker">Advanced Data Engineering with Databricks</div><h1><span class="kicker-inline">Recap</span>Databricks Performance Optimization</h1><div class="chips"><span class="chip">Course 3 of 4</span><span class="chip">⏱ ~9 minutes</span></div><p class="sub">Why queries are slow and what to do about it: <strong>file layout and data skipping</strong>, the classic Spark problems (<strong>skew, shuffle, spill, serialization</strong>), and choosing <strong>compute</strong>.</p></div></div><div class="idea"><span class="idea-icon">💡</span><div><b>The one idea to remember:</b> first <strong>read less data</strong> (good layout, data skipping), then <strong>move less data</strong> (avoid shuffles, broadcast small sides), and only then <strong>add hardware</strong>. The query profile and the Spark UI tell you which problem you have.</div></div>
