# MAGIC <div class="dbx">
# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">01</span><span class="sec-icon">🗺️</span><h2>What we covered</h2></div><div class="tbl"><table>
# MAGIC <thead>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <th>Topic</th>
# MAGIC <th>Key takeaway</th>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </thead>
# MAGIC <tbody>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td>Spark architecture</td>
# MAGIC <td>Driver, executors, <strong>jobs → stages → tasks</strong>. Shuffles create stage boundaries</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td>File layout</td>
# MAGIC <td>Small files, <strong>data skipping</strong> with file statistics, partitioning vs Z-order vs <strong>liquid clustering</strong></td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td>Managed maintenance</td>
# MAGIC <td><code>OPTIMIZE</code>, <code>VACUUM</code>, optimized writes, auto compaction, <strong>predictive optimization</strong></td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td>Skew</td>
# MAGIC <td>One task takes much longer than the rest. Fix it with AQE, salting, or filtering hot keys</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td>Shuffle</td>
# MAGIC <td>Wide transformations move data across the network. Broadcast joins avoid it</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td>Spill</td>
# MAGIC <td>Not enough memory per task, so data goes to disk. Fix it with more or smaller partitions or bigger nodes</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td>Serialization</td>
# MAGIC <td>Python UDFs are slow. Prefer <strong>built-in functions</strong>, then pandas UDFs</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td>Compute &amp; diagnostics</td>
# MAGIC <td>Cluster sizing, <strong>Photon</strong>, serverless, <strong>query profile</strong>, <strong>Spark UI</strong>, caching</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </tbody>
# MAGIC </table></div>
# MAGIC </div>

