# MAGIC <div class="dbx">
# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">02</span><span class="sec-icon">⚙️</span><h2>How Spark executes a query</h2></div><pre class="diagram">Query ─► Job ─► Stage 1 (scan, filter, project)  ─┐ shuffle (exchange)
# MAGIC                                                   ├► Stage 2 (join / aggregate) ─► write
# MAGIC                                                   │
# MAGIC          one task per partition, run in parallel on executor cores</pre>
# MAGIC <ul>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Narrow</strong> transformations (<code>filter</code>, <code>select</code>, <code>withColumn</code>) stay in the same stage.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Wide</strong> transformations (<code>groupBy</code>, <code>join</code>, <code>distinct</code>, <code>orderBy</code>) need a <strong>shuffle</strong>, which starts a new stage.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Adaptive Query Execution (AQE)</strong>, on by default, re-plans at stage boundaries using real data sizes:</li>
# MAGIC <li>switches to a <strong>broadcast join</strong>;</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>coalesces</strong> small partitions;</li>
# MAGIC <li>splits <strong>skewed</strong> partitions.</li>
# MAGIC </ul>
# MAGIC </div>

