# MAGIC <div class="dbx">
# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">03</span><span class="sec-icon">🗂️</span><h2>File layout and data skipping</h2></div><p>Delta stores <strong>min/max statistics</strong> per file, so a selective filter can <strong>skip files</strong>. That only works when similar values sit in the same files.</p>
# MAGIC <div class="tbl"><table>
# MAGIC <thead>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <th>Technique</th>
# MAGIC <th>Use when</th>
# MAGIC <th>Notes</th>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </thead>
# MAGIC <tbody>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Liquid clustering</strong> <code>CLUSTER BY (cols)</code></td>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Default for new tables</strong>. Filter or join on 1–4 columns, any cardinality</td>
# MAGIC <td>Incremental, and keys can be changed without a rewrite</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong><code>CLUSTER BY AUTO</code></strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Managed tables with unknown or changing query patterns</td>
# MAGIC <td>Databricks picks the keys (needs predictive optimization)</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Partitioning</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Very large tables (many TB) with a <strong>low-cardinality</strong> column used for lifecycle (e.g. date), partitions ≥ ~1 GB</td>
# MAGIC <td>Over-partitioning leads to millions of small files</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Z-order</strong> (legacy)</td>
# MAGIC <td>Existing partitioned tables</td>
# MAGIC <td>Not incremental. Must be re-run on all data</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </tbody>
# MAGIC </table></div>
# MAGIC <div class="code"><div class="code-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="lang">SQL</span><button class="copy" type="button">copy</button></div><pre><span style="color: #FF7B72">CREATE</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">TABLE</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">sales</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">(sale_ts</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">TIMESTAMP</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">,</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">customer_id</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">BIGINT,</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">store_id</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">INT,</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">amount</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">DOUBLE)</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #FF7B72">CLUSTER</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">BY</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">(customer_id,</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">sale_ts);</span>
# MAGIC <span></span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #E6EDF3">OPTIMIZE</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">sales;</span><span style="color: #6E7681">                     </span><span style="color: #8B949E; font-style: italic">-- compacts small files and clusters new data</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #FF7B72">ANALYZE</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">TABLE</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">sales</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">COMPUTE</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">STATISTICS</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">FOR</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">ALL</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">COLUMNS;</span></pre></div>
# MAGIC <ul>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Small-file problem:</strong> many tiny files from streaming or over-partitioning mean slow listing and slow scans. Fix it with <code>OPTIMIZE</code>, auto compaction and optimized writes.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Predictive optimization</strong> on UC managed tables runs <code>OPTIMIZE</code>, <code>VACUUM</code> and <code>ANALYZE</code> for you.</li>
# MAGIC <li>Write predicates on the column itself (<code>sale_ts &gt;= '2026-01-01'</code>), not on a function of it (<code>date(sale_ts) = …</code>), so that skipping works.</li>
# MAGIC </ul>
# MAGIC </div>

