# MAGIC <div class="dbx">
# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">04</span><span class="sec-icon">🔥</span><h2>The four classic problems</h2></div><div class="tbl"><table>
# MAGIC <thead>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <th>Problem</th>
# MAGIC <th>Symptom in Spark UI / query profile</th>
# MAGIC <th>Fixes</th>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </thead>
# MAGIC <tbody>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Skew</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>One task runs far longer than the median. Rows per task are very uneven</td>
# MAGIC <td>AQE skew join (on by default), <strong>salting</strong> hot keys, filtering or handling NULL / "unknown" keys separately</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Shuffle</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Large <em>shuffle read/write</em> bytes, many exchanges</td>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Broadcast</strong> the small side, filter and select early, pre-aggregate, cluster on join keys</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Spill</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td><em>Spill (memory/disk)</em> &gt; 0 in sort, aggregate or join stages</td>
# MAGIC <td>More partitions (smaller tasks), memory-optimized nodes, less data per key</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Serialization</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Slow Python UDF stages, Photon falls back</td>
# MAGIC <td>Replace UDFs with <strong>built-in functions</strong>. Otherwise use <strong>pandas (vectorized) UDFs</strong></td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </tbody>
# MAGIC </table></div>
# MAGIC <div class="code"><div class="code-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="lang">PYTHON</span><button class="copy" type="button">copy</button></div><pre><span style="color: #FF7B72">from</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">pyspark.sql</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">import</span> <span style="color: #E6EDF3">functions</span> <span style="color: #FF7B72">as</span> <span style="color: #E6EDF3">F</span>
# MAGIC <span></span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #8B949E; font-style: italic"># ❌ row-by-row Python UDF: data shipped to Python one row at a time</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #8B949E; font-style: italic"># clean = F.udf(lambda s: s.strip().lower())</span>
# MAGIC <span></span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #8B949E; font-style: italic"># ✅ built-in, runs in the JVM / Photon</span>
