# MAGIC <div class="dbx">
# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">05</span><span class="sec-icon">🔗</span><h2>Joins and shuffle partitions</h2></div><div class="tbl"><table>
# MAGIC <thead>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <th>Join strategy</th>
# MAGIC <th>When</th>
# MAGIC <th>Cost</th>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </thead>
# MAGIC <tbody>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Broadcast hash join</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>One side is small (under <code>spark.sql.autoBroadcastJoinThreshold</code>, or AQE decides at runtime)</td>
# MAGIC <td><strong>No shuffle</strong> of the big side, the fastest option</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td>Shuffle hash join</td>
# MAGIC <td>Medium side fits in memory per partition</td>
# MAGIC <td>One shuffle</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Sort-merge join</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Both sides large</td>
# MAGIC <td>Shuffle <strong>and</strong> sort on both sides</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </tbody>
# MAGIC </table></div>
# MAGIC <ul>
# MAGIC <li><code>spark.sql.shuffle.partitions</code> (default 200): with AQE, set it high (or <code>auto</code>) and let coalescing shrink it.</li>
# MAGIC <li>Too few partitions give huge tasks and spill. Too many give scheduling overhead and tiny output files.</li>
# MAGIC <li>Missing statistics can hide a broadcast opportunity. Run <code>ANALYZE TABLE</code>, or add a <code>/*+ BROADCAST(dim) */</code> hint.</li>
# MAGIC </ul>
# MAGIC </div>

