# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">06</span><span class="sec-icon">🖥️</span><h2>Compute choices</h2></div><div class="tbl"><table>
# MAGIC <thead>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <th>Choice</th>
# MAGIC <th>Guidance</th>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </thead>
# MAGIC <tbody>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Serverless</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Default for jobs, pipelines and SQL: fast start, auto-scaling, no tuning</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Photon</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Vectorized engine for SQL and DataFrame workloads. Big gains on scans, joins, aggregations and Delta writes</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td>Node type</td>
# MAGIC <td>Memory-optimized for large shuffles, joins and caching. Compute-optimized for CPU-heavy transforms. Storage-optimized (local SSD) for the <strong>disk cache</strong></td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td>Autoscaling</td>
# MAGIC <td>Good for variable load. Fixed size for steady streaming workloads</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td>Job clusters</td>
# MAGIC <td>Production jobs. All-purpose clusters are for interactive work</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </tbody>
# MAGIC </table></div>
# MAGIC <p><strong>Caching:</strong>
# MAGIC - <strong>Disk cache</strong>: automatic on SSD-backed nodes and SQL warehouses, and always consistent.
# MAGIC - <strong>Spark cache</strong> (<code>df.cache()</code>): manual, uses executor memory, and can go stale.
# MAGIC - <strong>Query result cache</strong>: repeated identical SQL queries.</p>
# MAGIC </div>

